/srv/git/3tched-container` (similar to `/srv/git/3tched.com` for the UI).\n  4. Hackathon Vision ($250k Prize):\n     - The architecture targets decentralized, OSCAL-compliant real estate smart contracts and peer-to-peer property settlement on Ethereum, competing against centralized monopolies (MLS / title cartels / centralized fractional platforms like Jeff Bezos's Arrived).\n     - Multi-tenancy operates as a **conglomerate / org-chart / hub-and-spoke**:\n       - **The Hub**: Central engine (stateless Qdrant, multi-tenant EMQX broker, shared Cozo public graph / OSCAL taxonomy).\n       - **The Spokes**: Individual sovereign container instances (their own WireGuard key, private ext4 Cozo data space, private Btrfs leaf sprout).\n       - Governed by an org-chart / conglomerate hierarchy with 2-of-N cryptographic superadmin gates.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Created & Initialized Dedicated Container Repo**:\n  - Initialized Git repository at `/srv/git/3tched-container` on branch `main` (commit `6760459`).\n  - Created:\n    - `profiles/3tched-lungs.json`: Native JSON profile for Incus defining `/dev/fuse`, `/run/opdbus/lungs` disk mount, and tmpfs `/run`.\n    - `instances/chatbot-template.json`: Parameterized JSON template with seccomp ioctl deny filters, UTS namespacing, and identity device bindings.\n    - `storage/make-cozo-device.sh`: Standalone script to create the 20 GiB sparse image with `p1` (10 GiB Btrfs leaf for `device add`) and `p2` (10 GiB ext4 pre-formatted for Cozo RocksDB with allocate-on-write).\n    - `scripts/launch-identity.sh`: JSON-driven launcher that queries Incus REST API, attaches the Cozo storage device, boots the container, and runs `btrfs device add` inside the container namespace.\n    - `README.md`: Complete documentation on architecture, nested Btrfs avoidance, and usage.\n- **Verified Seed Rootfs & Subvolumes (Read-Only)**:\n  - Loop-mounted `/var/lib/incus/storage-pools/3tched/3tched-seed.img1` read-only on `/mnt`:\n    - Verifi